ital banking services. In addition to BLIK, Spółdzielcza Grupa Bankowa offers a variety of other mobile payment options to cater to the diverse needs of its customers. These include Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, Fitbit Pay, and Xiaomi Pay, reflecting the bank's commitment to providing modern and convenient financial services. Through these offerings, Spółdzielcza Grupa Bankowa demonstrates its dedication to innovation and customer satisfaction in the rapidly evolving financial technology landscape.", "TOYOTA BANK:Toyota Bank is a bank in Poland offering Google Pay", "SWATCH PAY!:A mobile payment system available in some banks in Poland", "SAMSUNG PAY:", "AJZEN:Ajzen is a prominent theorist renowned for his significant contributions to the field of psychology, particularly in understanding human behavior and decision-making processes. He is best known for developing the Theory of Planned Behavior, a framework that has been extensively utilized to comprehend various aspects of consumer behavior, including the acceptance of mobile banking technologies. This theory posits that an individual's intention to engage in a behavior is influenced by their attitude towards the behavior, subjective norms, and perceived behavioral control. These components collectively help predict and explain why individuals decide to adopt or reject new technologies.\n\nIn addition to the Theory of Planned Behavior, Ajzen's work on the Theory of Reasoned Action is also highly influential. This earlier theory laid the groundwork for the Technology Acceptance Model, which is widely used to assess how users come to accept and use technology. The Theory of Reasoned Action suggests that a person's behavioral intentions are shaped by their attitudes towards the behavior and the subjective norms surrounding it. This model has been instrumental in understanding the factors that drive technology adoption and has been applied in various contexts, including information systems and consumer technology.\n\nOverall, Ajzen's theories have provided a robust framework for researchers and practitioners to analyze and predict human behavior in relation to technology and other domains. His work continues to be a cornerstone in the study of behavioral intentions and technology acceptance, influencing a wide range of fields from psychology to marketing and information systems."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_b4ca2775f1b54551e0522e2f4340c186405413ecf61079cb7d05d62a59536759_v2"}